<task id="128b" project="customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>customer.bicep: wire Document Intelligence + App Insights + Log Analytics + Redis -- closes the E1/E2 escalation gap task 127/128/129 flagged as out-of-scope</title>
    <phase>Phase C'' Wave G-2.5 -- customer.bicep completion (Path 1 owner decision; E1/E2 follow-on POML authored 2026-08-19 during task 128's authoring)</phase>
    <gate>cleared</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Owner-directed FULL, matching 127/128/129's rigor (customer.bicep is the LIVE production ARM template task 123's ArmDeploymentRunner deploys via the real Azure SDK -- a mistake here is deploy-blast-radius). Independently justified: this task also reverses a versioned (v3.2) documented architecture decision for Redis (see escalation trigger 1) -- FULL rigor's code-review + adr-check gate is the correct place to confirm that reversal is intentional before it ships.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Mechanical wiring of THREE ALREADY-BUILT, ALREADY-CORRECT modules (doc-intelligence.bicep, monitoring.bicep, redis.bicep -- all grep-verified to exist and be unmodified since their authoring tasks) into an existing composition. No new Bicep design. Sonnet @ high, matching 127/128/129.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <deps>102, 103, 123, 127, 128</deps>
    <tags>bicep-authoring, azure-deployment, deploy</tags>
    <estimated-effort>5-7 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>During task 128's authoring (2026-08-19), the project owner reviewed two open findings and made two decisions this task implements:

E1 -- Both task 127's escalation trigger and task 128's escalation trigger independently flagged that spec.md FR-04 ("Six new module invocations vs current Provision-Customer.ps1 step 3: Cosmos DB + OpenAI + AI Search + Document Intelligence + App Insights/Log Analytics + optional SignalR") and design.md §7.2 rows 11-12 require Document Intelligence + App Insights/Log Analytics wired into customer.bicep, and that this was OUTSIDE both 127's and 128's declared scope. Both tasks explicitly deferred rather than silently expanding. Owner decision: author a dedicated follow-on POML (this task) rather than fold it into 127 or 128 after the fact.

E2 -- Task 129 (kv-secrets wiring) independently flagged that manifest.yaml's `Redis-ConnectionString` `FromBicepOutput` classification conflicts with the documented per-environment (not per-customer) Redis architecture (Q-E FR-12 / design.md §7.2's disposition table, which marks Redis "shared | shared" across BOTH Model 1 and Model 2). Task 129 raised this as an unresolved escalation trigger rather than picking a path unilaterally. Owner clarification (2026-08-19, relayed for this task's authoring): "Redis is per-env, but in Model 2 (dedicated) env=customer, so Redis IS a per-customer resource in customer.bicep." Because customer.bicep is confirmed (per task 129's own background section) to be the SOLE template task 123's ArmDeploymentRunner deploys in production, and that deployment is exclusively the Model2Dedicated branch, the owner's reconciliation is: for THIS template specifically, "per environment" and "per customer" are the same unit, so wiring `modules/redis.bicep` into customer.bicep does not create a second, redundant Redis resource -- it IS the per-environment Redis for that customer's dedicated environment.

Grep-verified: `modules/doc-intelligence.bicep`, `modules/monitoring.bicep` (combines App Insights + Log Analytics in one module), and `modules/redis.bicep` already exist, are correct, and are currently ORPHANED as far as customer.bicep is concerned (customer.bicep's own header comment + an inline comment in its Cosmos DB section explicitly say per-customer Redis was REMOVED in a prior project, `spaarke-redis-cache-remediation-r2` task 020 -- those two comments are now STALE as of this task landing and MUST be corrected at the point of change, not left to drift, per this project's standing "fix drift at time of discovery" operating rule). Wire these three EXISTING modules into customer.bicep. Do NOT author new files (`modules/customer-docintel.bicep` / `modules/customer-monitoring.bicep` / `modules/customer-redis.bicep`) -- that would violate CLAUDE.md §11's reuse mandate against code that already exists, is correct, and is purpose-built for this exact call site.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in Bicep module composition, ADR-028 UAMI-only RBAC binding, honest-signal discipline (no fabricated secret outputs), and design.md §7 resource-naming/deployment-order conformance.</role>

  <goal>customer.bicep provisions a per-customer Document Intelligence account (RBAC-granted to the per-customer UAMI), a per-customer Log Analytics workspace + App Insights instance (via the single `monitoring.bicep` module), and -- per the owner's E2 reconciliation -- a per-customer Redis cache sized for dev/test cost by default and overridable for staging/prod, all wired WITHOUT disturbing task 127's App Service zone or task 128's OpenAI/AI Search zone. The two stale "Redis removed / not provisioned per-customer" comments already in customer.bicep are corrected in the same change so the file stops contradicting its own contents.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Tasks 127 and 128 (both same-day, 2026-08-19) each independently flagged this exact gap (Document Intelligence + App Insights/Log Analytics) via their own escalation triggers and declined to silently expand scope. Task 129 (kv-secrets wiring, not yet executed) independently flagged the Redis architecture question the same way. Rather than let three separate "not my scope" flags sit unresolved, the owner reviewed all three during task 128's authoring and directed: author ONE new POML (this task) covering all four remaining resources, grouped together because all four are supporting-infra wiring of the same shape (invoke an existing, correct, orphaned module; add per-customer naming; wire RBAC where the module supports it; add non-secret outputs only).</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">infrastructure/bicep/customer.bicep</file>
      <file role="modify">infrastructure/bicep/customer.json (regenerate via az bicep build --outfile)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">infrastructure/bicep/modules/doc-intelligence.bicep (DO NOT MODIFY, invoke as-is; already has a `userAssignedIdentityPrincipalId` param wired for Cognitive Services User RBAC, same pattern as openai.bicep/ai-search.bicep from task 128)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">infrastructure/bicep/modules/monitoring.bicep (DO NOT MODIFY, invoke as-is; single module emits BOTH the Log Analytics workspace AND the App Insights instance wired to it via `WorkspaceResourceId`; no UAMI RBAC param -- App Insights auth is connection-string/instrumentation-key based, not MI-based, so there is nothing to grant)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">infrastructure/bicep/modules/redis.bicep (DO NOT MODIFY, invoke as-is; FR-09 hardened module -- allkeys-lru eviction, TLS 1.2 min, optional VNet injection/RDB persistence; no UAMI RBAC param -- Redis auth is access-key based)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">infrastructure/bicep/parameters/redis-dev.bicepparam (dev-cost-optimized precedent: `sku='Basic'`, `capacity=0` -- ~$15/mo; this task's customer.bicep-level default should mirror this cost posture per the "dev-appropriate SKU" acceptance criterion, same pattern as task 127's `appServiceSku` default `'S1'` being a single overridable default rather than environment-conditional logic inside the template)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">infrastructure/bicep/stacks/model2-full.bicep lines 82-123, 378-421 (proven monitoring/redis/docIntelligence wiring shape; stack itself stale/CI-uncompiled per task 117, wiring shape is correct and is this task's SHAPE reference, not a file to copy)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/tasks/127-customer-bicep-uami-and-appservice-modules-and-wiring.poml (this task's insertion-zone precedent + completed COMPLETION notes -- read to know customer.bicep's CURRENT shape after 127 landed)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/tasks/128-customer-bicep-openai-and-aisearch-modules-and-wiring.poml (this task's insertion-zone precedent + secret-output-hygiene precedent -- "Do NOT echo openAiKey / searchServiceAdminKey as top-level outputs... avoid a redundant secret-exposure surface" -- this task follows the SAME precedent for docIntelligenceKey / redis access keys)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/tasks/129-customer-bicep-kv-secrets-generated-invocation-and-output-threading.poml (documents the EXACT 15-entry FromBicepOutput triage, including the 3 entries -- DocumentIntelligence-ApiKey, DocumentIntelligence-Endpoint, AppInsights-ConnectionString -- explicitly omitted BECAUSE these modules were not yet wired, plus the Redis-ConnectionString escalation this task's E2 reconciliation directly speaks to; if task 129 has not yet executed when this task lands, its 9-omitted-entry list is now partially stale -- see escalation trigger 3)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/design.md §7.1 (naming table -- has DocIntel/AppInsights/LogAnalytics rows, has NO Redis row -- v3.2 removed it), §7.2 (Resource Catalog rows 6 [struck], 11, 12; shared-vs-dedicated disposition table), §7.4/§7.5 (DocIntel config), §7.6 (Deployment Order steps 3, 8 [struck], 12), §7.7 (KV secret canonical names -- confirms AppInsights-ConnectionString / DocumentIntelligence-ApiKey / DocumentIntelligence-Endpoint are canonical secret names task 129 will eventually need)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/spec.md item 19 (v3.3 changelog line), FR-04, NFR-04, § MUST Rules ("MUST NOT provision Redis per-customer" -- v3.2 Q-E FR-12) -- ALL predate and conflict with the owner's E2 reconciliation; see escalation trigger 1</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/CLAUDE.md § MUST rules ("MUST NOT provision Redis per-customer (Q-E FR-12; per-env via Deploy-RedisCache.ps1)") -- same conflict, project-level restatement; see escalation trigger 1</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
