    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §11 (Component Justification -- Default to Reuse)">modules/doc-intelligence.bicep, modules/monitoring.bicep, and modules/redis.bicep already exist, are correct, and are purpose-built for exactly this per-customer stamp. MUST invoke these EXISTING modules unmodified. MUST NOT author new `modules/customer-*.bicep` files.</constraint>
    <constraint source="design.md §7.1 (authoritative naming table, v3.2)">Document Intelligence name MUST be `sprk-{customerId}-{environmentName}-docintel`; App Insights name MUST be `sprk-{customerId}-{environmentName}-insights`; Log Analytics name MUST be `sprk-{customerId}-{environmentName}-logs`. design.md §7.1 has NO Redis row (v3.2 removed it when Redis was struck from the per-customer catalog) -- this task's Redis name (`sprk-{customerId}-{environmentName}-redis`, matching the existing SignalR/OpenAI/AI Search naming shape already used elsewhere in customer.bicep) is NOT yet a canonical documented pattern. See escalation trigger 2.</constraint>
    <constraint source="design.md §7.5 + §7.2 row 11 (verified consistent -- do not re-derive)">Document Intelligence SKU MUST be `S0` (design.md's own stated default, matches doc-intelligence.bicep's module default -- do not override). Model config (`prebuilt-layout`) is consumed at the BFF application layer, not a Bicep param -- no action needed here.</constraint>
    <constraint source="design.md §7.2 row 12 (verified consistent -- do not re-derive)">App Insights + Log Analytics SKU/retention MUST be `PerGB2018` / 90-day retention -- matches monitoring.bicep's own module default (`retentionInDays int = 90`). Do NOT pass a custom `retentionInDays` override.</constraint>
    <constraint source="task 030 precedent / doc-intelligence.bicep's existing RBAC param">doc-intelligence.bicep already has a `userAssignedIdentityPrincipalId` param that grants Cognitive Services User (role `a97b65f3-24c7-4388-baec-2e87135dc908`) when non-empty, same pattern task 128 wired for openai.bicep/ai-search.bicep. Pass `uami.outputs.principalId` (task 127's uami module) into this invocation. monitoring.bicep and redis.bicep have NO UAMI RBAC param -- do NOT invent one; App Insights (connection-string/ikey auth) and Redis (access-key auth) are not MI-based in this codebase's current pattern.</constraint>
    <constraint source="Owner E2 reconciliation (binding for this task's Redis wiring -- see escalation trigger 1 for the unresolved doc-conflict this creates)">Wire `modules/redis.bicep` UNCONDITIONALLY into customer.bicep (no feature-gate param), matching Cosmos DB's unconditional-invocation precedent in the same file, because customer.bicep is confirmed (task 129's own background) to be the sole template deployed for the Model2Dedicated branch -- there is no Model 1 (shared) code path running through this file where "per-environment Redis" and "per-customer Redis" would diverge into two different resources.</constraint>
    <constraint source="redis-dev.bicepparam precedent + task 127's appServiceSku pattern (dev-appropriate default, single overridable value -- not environment-conditional Bicep logic)">Add `redisSku` (`@allowed(['Basic','Standard','Premium'])`, default `'Basic'`) and `redisCapacity` (`int`, default `0`) params to customer.bicep, mirroring `redis-dev.bicepparam`'s cost-optimized values. Staging/prod overrides happen via CLI `--parameters` or a future `.bicepparam` file at deploy time, matching how `appServiceSku`'s default `'S1'` is overridden today -- do NOT hardcode per-environment conditional logic inside customer.bicep itself.</constraint>
    <constraint source="task 128's secret-output-hygiene precedent (binding, applied consistently here)">Do NOT add new raw secret-bearing top-level customer.bicep outputs for this task's three modules: no `docIntelligenceKey`, no `redisPrimaryKey`, no `redisConnectionString` (Redis's connection string embeds the access key). Output ONLY non-secret identifiers/endpoints: `docIntelligenceEndpoint`, `docIntelligenceName`, `appInsightsName`, `appInsightsId`, `logAnalyticsName`, `logAnalyticsWorkspaceId`, `redisName`, `redisHostName`, `redisPort`. The underlying secret-bearing module outputs (`docIntelligence.outputs.docIntelligenceKey`, `monitoring.outputs.connectionString`, `redis.outputs.redisConnectionString`/`redisPrimaryKey`) remain available as in-file symbolic references for a FUTURE task-129-style kv-secrets amendment -- wiring them into `kv-secrets.generated.bicep`'s `secretValues` object is explicitly OUT OF SCOPE here (that is task 129's mandate). Do NOT silently touch task 129's file or POML.</constraint>
    <constraint source="Fix-drift-at-discovery (this project's standing operating rule + root CLAUDE.md §6.5 anti-silent-compliance)">customer.bicep currently carries TWO stale comments asserting Redis is deliberately NOT provisioned per-customer: the file-header comment (lines ~10-14, "Note: per-customer Redis is DEPRECATED per Q-E Architecture 1 / FR-12...") and an inline comment in the Cosmos DB section ("Redis is intentionally NOT provisioned per-customer (Q-E FR-12) -- see header note."). Both MUST be corrected (not left in place) as part of this change, replaced with an accurate statement of the E2 reconciliation + a forward-pointer to escalation trigger 1's unresolved spec.md/design.md conflict, so the file does not contradict its own contents the moment this task lands.</constraint>
    <constraint source="Parallel-safety with tasks 127/128's already-claimed zones (both landed or landing before this task per its deps)">This task MUST NOT touch: (a) the RG→KeyVault gap or the post-SignalR→pre-OUTPUTS App Service zone (task 127's insertion zones), or (b) the section task 128 inserts immediately after Cosmos DB and before Membership Topic (OpenAI + AI Search). This task's own insertion zones are: (i) a NEW Monitoring section (App Insights + Log Analytics) immediately after the Key Vault module and before Storage Account -- closest available position to design.md §7.6 step 3's early placement without reordering already-shipped modules; (ii) a NEW Document Intelligence section immediately AFTER task 128's AI Search module invocation, still before Membership Topic -- groups with the other AI resources per design.md §7.6's 10-11-12 (OpenAI → AI Search → DocIntel) adjacency; (iii) a NEW Redis section immediately after this task's own Document Intelligence section, still before Membership Topic. Read customer.bicep AS IT STANDS after task 128 has landed before choosing exact insertion points -- do not assume line numbers from this POML's authoring-time read.</constraint>
  </constraints>

