  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Rigor + load">Emit RIGOR LEVEL (FULL). Read customer.bicep as it stands after tasks 127+128 land, doc-intelligence.bicep, monitoring.bicep, redis.bicep, redis-dev.bicepparam, design.md §7.1/§7.2/§7.4-7.7, and this project's spec.md/CLAUDE.md MUST-rule lines on Redis (needed for escalation trigger 1's exact citation).</step>
    <step order="1" name="Correct the two stale Redis comments">Before adding any new resource, rewrite customer.bicep's file-header Redis note and the Cosmos-DB-section inline Redis note to reflect the E2 reconciliation (per-customer Redis now wired for this Model2Dedicated-only template) + a pointer to this task's escalation trigger 1 (the unresolved spec.md/design.md v3.2 conflict this reconciliation creates). Do not simply delete the history -- state what changed and why, so a future reader is not left to re-derive it.</step>
    <step order="2" name="Monitoring (App Insights + Log Analytics)">Add a new section immediately after the Key Vault module, before Storage Account, invoking `modules/monitoring.bicep` with `appInsightsName: 'sprk-${customerId}-${environmentName}-insights'`, `logAnalyticsName: 'sprk-${customerId}-${environmentName}-logs'`, `location`, `tags` (no `retentionInDays` override -- module default 90 already matches design.md).</step>
    <step order="3" name="Document Intelligence">Add a new section immediately after task 128's AI Search module invocation (still before Membership Topic), invoking `modules/doc-intelligence.bicep` with `docIntelligenceName: 'sprk-${customerId}-${environmentName}-docintel'`, `location`, `sku: 'S0'`, `userAssignedIdentityPrincipalId: uami.outputs.principalId`, `tags`.</step>
    <step order="4" name="Redis">Add a new section immediately after this task's Document Intelligence section (still before Membership Topic), invoking `modules/redis.bicep` with `redisName: 'sprk-${customerId}-${environmentName}-redis'`, `location`, `sku: redisSku`, `capacity: redisCapacity`, `tags` (new `redisSku`/`redisCapacity` params per this POML's constraints, default `'Basic'`/`0`). Leave `subnetId`/`staticIP` at module defaults (customer.bicep has no VNet module -- public network access is correct here, matching Cosmos DB / OpenAI / AI Search's own public-endpoint posture in this file).</step>
    <step order="5" name="Outputs">Add, under the non-secret names listed in this POML's secret-output-hygiene constraint: `docIntelligenceEndpoint`, `docIntelligenceName`, `appInsightsName`, `appInsightsId`, `logAnalyticsName`, `logAnalyticsWorkspaceId`, `redisName`, `redisHostName`, `redisPort`. Do NOT add `docIntelligenceKey`, `redisPrimaryKey`, or `redisConnectionString` as top-level outputs.</step>
    <step order="6" name="Validate">`az bicep build --file infrastructure/bicep/customer.bicep --outfile infrastructure/bicep/customer.json` -- 0 errors, 0 net-new warnings vs the pre-task file (diff against `git show HEAD:infrastructure/bicep/customer.bicep` per task 127's verified-clean-diff precedent). Commit the regenerated customer.json alongside customer.bicep.</step>
    <step order="7" name="What-if (or documented deferral)">If live Azure reachability is available, run `az deployment sub what-if` against a throwaway `customerId`/`environmentName` at subscription scope and confirm the 3 new resources (Document Intelligence, monitoring's Log Analytics + App Insights, Redis) show as Create with no unexpected changes to the resources tasks 127/128 already landed. If not reachable, document as deferred to a live ceremony, per the precedent set by tasks 108/123/125/127.</step>
    <step order="8" name="Spec.md + design.md v3.3 amendment (Path B fold-in per owner 2026-08-19)">Owner confirmed 2026-08-19 (via AskUserQuestion) that E2's Redis reconciliation IS the intended reversal + the amendment is FOLDED INTO this task per CLAUDE.md §6.5 Path B. Amendments (all in one commit alongside the Bicep changes above):
    (a) **spec.md item 19** (v3.3 changelog line): add a new entry "Redis reinstated as per-customer for Model 2 (dedicated only) per env=customer 1:1 semantics; Model 1 shared-Redis unchanged. Reverses v3.2 blanket-shared decision. Owner-confirmed 2026-08-19. Task 128b."
    (b) **spec.md FR-04**: update the Redis line so it distinguishes Model 1 (shared, platform-provisioned) from Model 2 (per-customer, customer.bicep-provisioned).
    (c) **spec.md § MUST Rules**: change the "MUST NOT provision Redis per-customer" bullet to "MUST NOT provision Redis per-customer FOR MODEL 1" — the Model 2 case now MUST provision Redis per-customer (which is per-env since env=customer).
    (d) **design.md §7.2 Resource Catalog row 6**: unstrike the Redis row for Model 2; keep struck (or mark "Model 1 only") the shared-Redis reference. Add a note citing the E2 reconciliation.
    (e) **design.md §7.2 shared-vs-dedicated disposition table**: change the Redis row from "🔵 shared | shared" to "🔵 shared (Model 1) | 🟢 dedicated per-customer (Model 2)".
    (f) **design.md §7.6 step 8**: unstrike for Model 2; note it stays struck for Model 1.
    (g) **design.md §7.7**: update the `redis-connection-string` line — Model 1 drops it (still uses platform-KV reference); Model 2 restores it as a per-customer KV entry (task 129 territory).
    (h) **projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/CLAUDE.md § MUST rules**: change "MUST NOT provision Redis per-customer (Q-E FR-12; per-env via Deploy-RedisCache.ps1)" to distinguish the two models (Model 1 = per-env-shared; Model 2 = per-customer-dedicated).
    (i) **Bump spec.md and design.md version** to v3.3; add version bump line to each file's header.
    All amendments MUST be committed in the SAME PR (same commit is preferred) as the Bicep changes, so the docs stop contradicting the code at the moment of merge. This is a Path B amendment, not silent violation.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <!-- RESOLVED 2026-08-19 via AskUserQuestion: owner confirmed Path B amendment folded INTO this task's step 8. Trigger 1 below is preserved for historical context on WHY the amendment is needed; the executor does NOT need to re-STOP-and-confirm. Triggers 2/3/4 remain live. -->
    <trigger>The owner's E2 Redis reconciliation directly reverses a VERSIONED (v3.2), multiply-cited, and detailed prior architecture decision -- not a stale/ambiguous doc-comment. Specifically: (a) spec.md item 19 ("Redis removed per Q-E FR-12 (v3.2 -- Redis is per-env...)"), spec.md FR-04 ("Redis explicitly NOT provisioned"), spec.md § MUST Rules ("MUST NOT provision Redis per-customer"); (b) design.md §7.2's Resource Catalog row 6 struck through with "REMOVED v3.2 (M-1 / Q-E FR-12)" AND its shared-vs-dedicated disposition table explicitly marking Redis "🔵 Per-environment... shared | shared" for BOTH Model 1 AND Model 2 (dedicated) -- i.e. design.md's own v3.2 authors already considered the Model-2-dedicated case and still concluded "shared", the opposite of this task's premise; design.md §7.6 step 8 struck through; design.md §7.7 ("`redis-connection-string` DROPPED -- Redis is per-env now; BFF app-settings reference the per-env Redis secret in the platform KV, not per-customer"); (c) this project's own CLAUDE.md § MUST rules, same statement. STOP and confirm with the project owner, BEFORE this task's Redis wiring is dispatched for execution, that the E2 reconciliation is intended to REVERSE all of the above rather than merely clarify an edge case -- and if confirmed, this is a Path B (ADR/spec amendment) situation per root CLAUDE.md §6.5: author a spec.md/design.md v3.3 amendment (updating item 19, FR-04, the MUST-rule bullet, §7.2's catalog row + disposition table, §7.6 step 8, §7.7) that lands EITHER before or in the SAME PR as this task's Bicep change, so the documents stop contradicting the code the moment this task merges. Do not let this task's Bicep changes ship with spec.md/design.md still asserting the opposite.</trigger>
    <trigger>This task's Redis naming (`sprk-{customerId}-{environmentName}-redis`) and SKU defaults (`Basic`/`0`) are this task's own choice, not sourced from an existing design.md §7.1 row (v3.2 removed Redis from that table entirely). If the spec.md/design.md v3.3 amendment in escalation trigger 1 is authored, it MUST also add a Redis row back to §7.1's naming table and confirm (or correct) this task's naming/SKU choice -- do not treat this task's naming as retroactively canonical without that amendment landing.</trigger>
    <trigger>If task 129 has NOT yet executed when this task lands, task 129's documented 9-entry "not resolvable" kv-secrets omission list (DocumentIntelligence-ApiKey, DocumentIntelligence-Endpoint, AppInsights-ConnectionString, and -- pending escalation trigger 1's resolution -- Redis-ConnectionString) is now PARTIALLY STALE: this task wires the underlying modules those 3-4 entries needed. Flag to whoever dispatches task 129 that its POML's step 1 triage + acceptance-criteria 6-key/9-key split should be RE-VERIFIED against customer.bicep's actual post-128b state before execution, rather than executed as originally authored. Do NOT silently amend task 129's POML from within this task -- that is a separate, explicit authoring action for the project owner/dispatcher to take.</trigger>
    <trigger>If task 129 HAS already executed by the time this task lands (race), its `kvSecretValues` object will have already omitted these entries per its original (now-partially-stale) triage -- confirm with the project owner whether a task-129-amendment follow-on is warranted to pick up the newly-resolvable entries, rather than leaving them permanently omitted.</trigger>
  </escalation>

